cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "PSC Digital Twin: a climate-aware Gaussian-process surrogate for perovskite solar cell degradation"
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tippin
    given-names: Favian
    affiliation: Arizona State University
abstract: >
  An open web application that replaces expensive COMSOL drift-diffusion
  simulations of perovskite solar cell degradation with a Gaussian-process
  surrogate trained on a 36-run full-factorial illumination/temperature
  campaign. Full J-V curves are predicted through a proper-orthogonal-
  decomposition basis with Gaussian-process mode coefficients. The application
  reports calibrated predictive uncertainty, refuses to produce numbers outside
  its validated design envelope, and recommends the next most informative
  simulation to run.
keywords:
  - perovskite solar cells
  - surrogate modeling
  - Gaussian process
  - proper orthogonal decomposition
  - digital twin
  - photovoltaic degradation
  - active learning
license: MIT
